1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,098
Day 58: OpenSRE, a self-hosted agent that investigates CI

2
00:00:05,098 --> 00:00:05,904
failures.

3
00:00:05,904 --> 00:00:10,286
We ran it on a local model, with no paid API key.

4
00:00:10,736 --> 00:00:11,978
You hand it an alert.

5
00:00:11,978 --> 00:00:15,347
It plans what to check, gathers evidence from your tools,

6
00:00:15,347 --> 00:00:17,180
and writes a root cause report.

7
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:20,939
We broke a tiny repo by swapping round for int,

8
00:00:20,939 --> 00:00:22,065
which truncates.

9
00:00:22,065 --> 00:00:24,248
The CI log went into the alert.

10
00:00:24,698 --> 00:00:26,259
The planner picks tools.

11
00:00:26,259 --> 00:00:28,210
Log tools need Datadog or AWS,

12
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:31,397
and the code runner was called without arguments.

13
00:00:31,847 --> 00:00:33,746
So the loop ran five times,

14
00:00:33,746 --> 00:00:36,560
and every evidence step came back empty.

15
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:39,785
All four runs called it a code defect,

16
00:00:39,785 --> 00:00:41,976
but none found the truncation.

17
00:00:41,976 --> 00:00:44,678
On CPU, the 14B model never finished,

18
00:00:44,678 --> 00:00:47,599
because of a fixed sixty second timeout.

19
00:00:48,049 --> 00:00:50,104
Apache-2.0, self-hosted.

20
00:00:50,104 --> 00:00:53,958
Logs and the write-up are on Zenn and GitHub.
